<title>SWEDEN: SKF sees no sign of upturn in W.Europe.</title>
<headline>SKF sees no sign of upturn in W.Europe.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's SKF, the world's largest bearings maker, on Tuesday posted a 38 percent fall in profits for the first quarter of 1997, saying it saw no sign of a significant upturn in market conditions in Western Europe.</p>
<p>SKF reported a profit after financial items of 501 million crowns ($65.4 million) in the three months ending March 31 when sales dipped to 8.86 billion crowns from 8.88 billion crowns a year earlier.</p>
<p>($ = 7.663 Swedish Crowns)</p>
